# 0.1.19: RAC-Board's Weapons on the board (the owner: "make the board compatible with weapons/gadgets as well, so
# weapons can be used/equipped while riding. including wrench"), first person, on Novalis by the crate class 511
# (QUEST_SIM_NEAR, as wrench.sim) with the Blaster in the hand (QUEST_SIM_GIVE=15,12,16,10 QUEST_SIM_HOLD=15). The board
# out as racboard.sim does it (the right hand behind the back, its stick clicked), and while riding: the right trigger
# fires the Blaster ("[sim] item 15: ... rounds" falls); B spins (RAC-Board's trick); the right grip takes the wrench
# out and fast strokes across swing it by hand ([vr-wrench] lines); the grip let go, the trigger takes the Blaster back
# out and fires again. The weapon wheel opened while riding (the right stick's click, the hand ahead) and its top icon
# taken: "[vr-ring]" lines, the pick out (Swap at full speed). The left hand's reach puts the board away. RAC-Board's
# log: "Weapons on the board: the game's item update found"; its trace (settings "trace"): its states. QUEST_JET_TRACE:
# riding from the click to the left reach, not off between. With "weapons": false (racboardweapons-off) the wrench is
# put away on the board and nothing fires, as before 0.1.19.
